From 7e987f5240570e70828cb404524619a652bb3b30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hq <hq@arifilabs>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 21:40:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix the merge so it builds: 5 files, 6 defects

Found by compiling, in order:

vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp - drop turbo3_0 from the non-SET_ROWS copy_to_quant emission list. The
fork's own comment two lines below says that variant is omitted because the plain quantize() path
lacks the WHT transform. The merge kept the comment and the standalone copy-from-quant line but
left turbo3_0 in the loop.

ggml-vulkan.cpp - remove the pipeline registration for cpy_f32_turbo3_0, which referenced a shader
that is now never generated. Comment left at the site so it is not "fixed" back in.

models.h / mtmd-image.cpp - Muse Glimmer landed three times: clip_graph_muse_glimmer,
muse_glimmer_grid_size and the preprocessor were each defined 3x. All copies byte-identical, kept
one of each. The duplicate came from one commit being emitted into several patch layers.

server-context.cpp - two definitions of server_prepare_shared_draft_devices coexisted, one
returning the new config struct and one returning bool. Overload resolution chose the bool one
because the call site passes a non-const reference. Removed the superseded version.

server-context.cpp - prompt_checkpoint_restored had landed as a READ only. Four other sites were
missing: the declaration, the clear in reset(), the has_checkpoint_restored_prompt predicate with
its guard in the generating pass, the set on restore, and the clear after batching. Declaring the
field alone would have compiled clean and left the guard permanently false, silently disabling the
restored-checkpoint protection. A partial merge that builds is the dangerous shape.
